#+TITLE: XRecord ENTMAKEX drops valid code-102 list payload (SCHMS PKPM)
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: master
#+DATE: 2026-10-27

* Reproducer -- no SCHMS dependency

Run from the repository root:

#+begin_src sh
clautolisp -norc --host cador -l issues/open/xrecord-102-payload-lost-repro.lsp -q
#+end_src

The attached source creates ONE free XRecord, reads its payload with ENTGET,
prints EXPECTED / ACTUAL and PASS / FAIL, then erases only its own object.
No drawing file, dictionary, SCHMS source, ALFE bridge or DWG codec is needed.

Expected:
#+begin_example
EXPECTED: ((102 . "{") (60 . 900) (60 . 1000) (102 . "}"))
ACTUAL: ((102 . "{") (60 . 900) (60 . 1000) (102 . "}"))
PASS: XRecord payload preserved
#+end_example

Observed with a fresh SBCL build of master =e98b17f2=, Clautolisp 2.3.72,
macOS (the same loss occurs in Linux SCHMS CI):
#+begin_example
EXPECTED: ((102 . "{") (60 . 900) (60 . 1000) (102 . "}"))
ACTUAL: nil
FAIL: XRecord payload lost
#+end_example

The installed Clautolisp 2.3.24 preserves the exact payload (PASS).
Additional isolation controls on 2.3.72: without 102 delimiters, the repeated
=(60 . 900)= and =(60 . 1000)= survive; inside ={ ... }=, even a string
=(1 . "value")= disappears. This is a lost 102 group, not integer precision
or a boolean representation difference.

* Code path and cause identified by inspection

=clautolisp/cador/source/entity-api.lisp=:
=al-data->pure= calls =%drop-view-only-groups=. This removes every group
recognised by =%reactor-group-start-p= until =%reactor-group-end-p=.
The start predicate accepts ANY code-102 string beginning with ={=,
including the plain ="{"= used by an XRecord's application payload.
Thus actual payload is discarded as if it were a synthesized ACAD_REACTORS
header. Distinguish genuine synthesized header groups from XRecord payload;
keep the existing ownership/reactor round-trip guarantees when fixing it.

* Real regression and engine evidence

SCHMS =src-vlx/xdata_codec.lsp= uses control code 102 to delimit lists in
XRecords. =src-vlx/test-cad-tables.lsp= detects the loss in:
- =postes-conservent-pkpm-booleen-et-reference= (900/1000 and 1900/2000);
- =remplacement-retire-reordonne-et-remplace= (4/104 and 1004/1104).

[[https://fabrik.sncf.fr/gitlab/dmoe-pop/epure/es/schms/-/jobs/554138][SCHMS Linux job 554138]],
pipeline 91127, source =a8c313cd=: 21/23 CAO tests, exactly these two fail
with Clautolisp 2.3.72. Also observed under 2.3.70 (job 554046).
Clautolisp 2.3.24 locally and 2.3.23 Windows pass these tests; AutoCAD passes
23/23. BricsCAD passes 23/23 (job 554200). Native optimized DES and VLX both
pass the 239 unit tests, so do not disable local binding optimization to hide
this independent Cador loss.

* Acceptance

The attached reproducer must print PASS; add automated coverage for free AND
dictionary-owned XRecords, nested 102 lists, ENTMAKE/ENTMAKEX and ENTMOD.
Retain genuine ACAD_REACTORS / extension-dictionary round-trip tests.
The original SCHMS CAO suite must return 23/23 with its expectations intact.
